And then you turn us back into light.

00:21:04.440 --> 00:21:24.050
I light your color notes out, Miss Frizzle.

00:21:24.740 --> 00:21:25.840
Why, thank you, Arnold.

00:21:26.570 --> 00:21:27.270
Let them out?

00:21:27.880 --> 00:21:29.840
What's that supposed to mean, hmm?

00:21:30.320 --> 00:21:32.100
We figured it out, Ms. Frizzle.

00:21:32.710 --> 00:21:35.570
All the colors of the rainbow are hidden in ordinary light.

00:21:36.860 --> 00:21:39.240
And you can use a prism to separate them out.

00:21:39.340 --> 00:21:44.140
If the colors of light back together, you get ordinary light again.

00:21:44.720 --> 00:21:47.530
Which means white light is just filled with color.

00:21:48.100 --> 00:21:51.150
So that's where color comes from. From light.

00:21:51.740 --> 00:21:56.160
Speaking about color and light, did you, um, make the rainbow?

00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:59.650
Because if you didn't, the pinball machine is mine.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:00.740
Oh, my.

